<mxfile host="65bd71144e">
    <diagram id="eCLYdJd_5VINLiGu_Vp_" name="Page-1">
        <mxGraphModel dx="2981" dy="1256" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="light-dark(#ffffff, #121212)" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="0"/>
                <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-10" edge="1" parent="1" source="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-1" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-11">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="210" y="560" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-1" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=30;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=1;roundedPerimeter=1;" value="TTY" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="120" width="350" x="250" y="400" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-2" parent="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-1" style="text;strokeColor=default;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;" value="1. it is a virtual console" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="30" width="350" y="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-9" parent="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-1" style="text;strokeColor=default;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(209, 215, 224); font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(33, 40, 48);&quot;&gt;Virtual console TTY: program ⇄ [TTY] ⇄ kernel driver ⇄ real keyboard + screen&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="60" width="350" y="60" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-7" edge="1" parent="1" source="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-5" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.25;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.25;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-8">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="1140" y="530" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-5" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=30;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=1;marginBottom=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=1;roundedPerimeter=1;" value="Pty" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="100" width="290" x="750" y="400" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-6" parent="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-5" style="text;strokeColor=default;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;rotatable=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=1 4;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(209, 215, 224); font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; background-color: rgb(33, 40, 48);&quot;&gt;PTY: program ⇄ [TTY (slave)] ⇄ [master] ⇄ another program (terminal app, sshd, tmux)&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="70" width="290" y="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-14" edge="1" parent="1" source="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-8" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-15">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="1250.0000000000005" y="709.9999999999998" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-8" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=light-dark(#FFFFFF,#FFFFFF);" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 192, 192); background-color: transparent; scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 192, 192); background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 192, 192); background-color: transparent; scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;&quot;ls -l&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 192, 192); background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; | &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(192, 192, 192); background-color: transparent; scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;bash // no pty required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20); background-color: light-dark(rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;scrollbar-color: rgba(168, 169, 170, 0.52) rgb(18, 19, 20);&quot;&gt;So the PTY is a compatibility layer. It exists so a program written for a 1970s serial terminal still works unchanged when the “terminal” is a window on your screen.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="120" width="330" x="1070" y="510" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-12" edge="1" parent="1" source="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-11" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-13">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="250" y="900" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-11" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=light-dark(#FFFFFF,#FFFFFF);" value="&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Linux virtual consoles are the text-based terminals you can access using keyboard shortcuts such as:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; padding: 0px; position: relative; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(33, 40, 48);&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Ctrl + Alt + F1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.25em; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Ctrl + Alt + F2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.25em; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Ctrl + Alt + F3&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;These correspond to devices such as:&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;/dev/tty1&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;/dev/tty2&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;/dev/tty3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="230" width="480" x="-10" y="610" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-13" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=light-dark(#FFFFFF,#FFFFFF);" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;When it’s actually useful&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;Rescuing a broken desktop. If your GUI won’t start after a bad driver or config change (a common one is NVIDIA drivers), switch to tty3 and fix it. You can reinstall packages, edit config files, or roll back an update.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;Killing a frozen desktop. If the screen is hung, Ctrl+Alt+F3, log in, then kill the stuck app or restart the display manager (sudo systemctl restart gdm, sddm, or lightdm).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;Running without a GUI. You can install updates, run builds, or run servers with less RAM and CPU used by the desktop.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;Several separate sessions. Each of tty1 to tty6 is its own login. You can run different things in each and switch with Ctrl+Alt+F1 through F6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;Learning and debugging. It’s a clean environment to see how the system behaves with no desktop in the way.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="290" width="520" x="-70" y="910" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-16" edge="1" parent="1" source="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-15" style="edgeStyle=none;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-17">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
                        <mxPoint x="1300.0000000000005" y="1070" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-15" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=light-dark(#FFFFFF,#FFFFFF);" value="&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;PTY does three jobs:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;1. Pretends to be a terminal device. The program sees /dev/pts/N and isatty() returns true.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;2. Carries data both ways. Your keystrokes go in, and the program’s output comes back out.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;3. Runs the kernel’s terminal logic in between. This is called the line discipline. It handles echo, backspace, Ctrl+C turning into a SIGINT signal, and raw vs. line mode. It also holds the window size (rows and columns).&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="200" width="450" x="1050" y="730" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="jLdWurAPai7qA6rNOrcB-17" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=light-dark(#FFFFFF,#FFFFFF);" value="&lt;h2 dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px; line-height: 1.25; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(61, 68, 77, 0.7); padding-bottom: 0.3em; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;why not to use tty directly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Because a real TTY’s other end is fixed hardware, and you can’t put your own program there.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; padding: 0px; position: relative; font-family: &amp;quot;Mona Sans VF&amp;quot;, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans Backtick Fix&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Noto Sans&amp;quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif, &amp;quot;Apple Color Emoji&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Emoji&amp;quot;; font-size: 14px; text-align: start; background-color: rgb(33, 40, 48); margin-bottom: 0px !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Limited number, tied to the physical machine.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;Linux has only a handful of virtual consoles (tty1 to tty6), all sharing one keyboard and one screen, and only one is visible at a time. You couldn’t have 20 terminal tabs, 50 SSH users, or a terminal per browser session.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.25em; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;The output goes to hardware, not to your program.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;If you write to /dev/tty3, the kernel sends the text to the screen. Your terminal app (iTerm, VS Code, a browser terminal) never sees it, so it can’t draw it in its own window. Likewise, keystrokes come from the physical keyboard, not from your app. There’s no place for a program to sit in the middle and say “I’ll provide the input and read the output.”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.25em; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;No remote access.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;When you SSH in, your keyboard is on another computer. The server’s kernel has no hardware path to it. sshd needs a terminal that it can feed with your keystrokes (received over the network) and read output from (to send back over the network). Only a PTY lets a program do that.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0.25em; margin-left: 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;p dir=&quot;auto&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: light-dark(rgb(33, 40, 48), rgb(0, 0, 0));&quot;&gt;Programs expect a TTY.&lt;br style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box;&quot;&gt;bash, vim and ssh need the terminal features we covered: raw mode, signals, window size. So you can’t just give them a plain pipe. You need something that is a TTY but is controlled by software.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="500" width="880" x="880" y="1050" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>